5. COMPUTE HALF TXC INDEPENDENTLY
==================================================

The remembered half wall needs its own texture X coordinate.

At the half-wall encounter, either:

A. compute and store the fractional coordinate immediately

or

B. store half distance/SID and derive it after the loop

using the same verified wall mathematics:

    SID=0:
        frac = PY + halfD*RY

    SID=1:
        frac = PX + halfD*RX

    frac = frac - INT(frac)

Then:

    halfTXC = INT(frac*64)

Apply the existing face-flip convention if the ordinary wall renderer already
uses one.

Do NOT reuse the final far-wall TXC.

